#: src/settings.php
msgid "With a key saved, the title and text of each published post without a password are sent to OpenAI, so Undergrowth can tell which of your posts are about similar things and suggest links between them. Nothing is sent until you save a key. Undergrowth changes a post only when you accept a link in it."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings.php
msgid "Questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings.php
msgid "With a key saved, Undergrowth asks Claude, through the Anthropic API, to write you an occasional question about your own writing. Each request sends one post’s title, a few sentences quoted from that post and, when the question comes from a reader’s comment, the text of that comment. A question about a gap between your posts quotes one sentence from each of up to three of them instead. Whole posts are never sent. A question about a post you moved to compost is sent back once more, on its own, to check it. Nothing is sent until you save a key. The questions appear only on your Dashboard, never to your readers."
msgstr ""

#: src/settings.php
msgid "Discord"
msgstr ""

#: src/settings.php
msgid "Optional. Undergrowth can post each new link suggestion to a channel in your own Discord server, with Accept and Veto buttons that work like the ones on Posts > Link suggestions. Each message sends Discord the titles of both posts, the suggested sentence, which is in your own words, and links to both posts. Nothing is sent until every Discord field on this page is filled in. Use a private channel: anyone who can read it sees your suggestions, and nothing is ever posted to your readers."
msgstr ""

